    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Expected lifecycle and move gap",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Expected transitions:** host names are never reused. Clean leaves, drains and world stop/start may temporarily make a host Deployment unready, remove a desired row, or create a replacement name. Treat short demand/object/Ready deltas as convergence, and defer policy interpretation to WorldHostsBelowReplicas, WorldFleetDown/Behind and the coordinator cut/succession view.\n\n**Explicit gap — occupied-land moves:** no scrapeable Elastic 5 move metrics exist, so this dashboard does not infer moves from logs, succession counts, generation, or land churn. A coordinator WorldLink is also not a peer-link metric; peer-specific instrumentation is not claimed here."
      }
    }
